{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-9-14","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：素数与互素与整数","englishTitle":"If a number be the least that is measured by prime numbers, it will not be measured by any other prime number except those originally measuring it.","book":9,"number":14,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.14","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.14/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":14,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","contentId":"euclid-9-14","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c9abd9eaa931fcda0e91b605af32895f8fcb17fb158a15e9b0a599f62b240610","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-9-14.statement","euclid-9-14.construction.1","euclid-9-14.proof.1","euclid-9-14.proof.2","euclid-9-14.proof.3","euclid-9-14.proof.4","euclid-9-14.proof.5","euclid-9-14.proof.6","euclid-9-14.conclusion","euclid-9-14.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-9-14.statement","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f8b4fa7a6b59add05be31ae68dbc577842dfad575b67927046de91490700d54f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If a number be the least that is measured by prime numbers, it will not be measured by any other prime number except those originally measuring it."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果一个数字是用素数整除的最低数值,除原先整除的数字外,将不用任何其他素数整除。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"30925b86aa719b58c0e341de0ab389cf4e23a8671eb316f7bde086cf046aa7f6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let the number A be the least that is measured by the prime numbers B, C, D; I say that A will not be measured by any other prime number except B, C, D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"A数字至少是用素数 B、C、D数字整除的;我说,A数字除B、C、D数字外,将不用其他任何素数数字整除。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"89335515f2cdc1ddc981a9ea93feb68d3e274e104a0003a02f28a086d40d3cab","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if possible, let it be measured by the prime number E, and let E not be the same with any one of the numbers B, C, D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能的话,用素数 E来整除,让E来计算,与B、C、D中的任何一个数字不同。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8022727ff7faad862b72f97d3f4ff5175f187bd22715348c418ca6f517d1147a","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now, since E measures A, let it measure it according to F; therefore E by multiplying F has made A."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,E 整除 A, 让它整除, F。 因此,E乘以F, 已经A。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"444e027a2a6c16addc138284f351dffda122029fe4b1e8f9f427c085db7d9d60","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And A is measured by the prime numbers B, C, D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"A是用素数 B,C,D整除的"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"4c2ec09e372e6ff5717652f43b9a2cd1b3bca9b8e72c8f895cafb460ffe372e0","citations":["euclid-7-30"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, if two numbers by multiplying one another make some number, and any prime number measure the product, it will also measure one of the original numbers; [[VII. 30](/principles/euclid-7-30)] therefore B, C, D will measure one of the numbers E, F."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,如果两个数字通过相互乘法 得出了一定的数字, 任何素数 整除 的产品, 它也会有整除 一个原始的数字。 因此,B, C, D 将整除 之一的E, F。 [[VII. 30](/principles/euclid-7-30)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"3026ef57ce67a1f3f0de4137017dccbf77d792c6f460078e04a335bb1bc078a4","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now they will not measure E; for E is prime and not the same with any one of the numbers B, C, D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在它们不会整除 E;E是首要的, 而不是B,C,D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"38c88f900347cc0b87854797e291a61141eb3f4b6b3f030d5a133ca6a4df048c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore they will measure F, which is less than A: which is impossible, for A is by hypothesis the least number measured by B, C, D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,它们将达到整除 F,不到A,这是不可能的,因为假设A的人数最少,为B、C、D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":8,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9e016f17b4ddbc4730729f38d9199aa80b4230be1ae511b5a4ee664065cf5d80","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore no prime number will measure A except B, C, D. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,除B、C、D、Q、E和D外,没有素数会整除 A。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-14.source","contentId":"euclid-9-14","revisionId":"euclid-9-14@raw-c9abd9eaa931fcda","order":9,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"01437061065d496316bfcd1df497d343ed3c31ff0e87f962793ff88d5ea8f1bc","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.14/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.14\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-9-14:euclid-7-30:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-9-14","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-9-14.proof.4"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-30","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.14","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.14/","sourceLabel":"VII. 30"}}],"incomingEdges":[],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-9-14:euclid-7-30:explicit","id":"euclid-7-30","book":7,"number":30,"kind":"proposition","title":"欧几里得引理：素数整除乘积必整除一个因子","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[],"visualization":{"level":"concept_illustration","rendererId":"concept-number","rationale":"The current renderer is selected by a broad geometry family and must not be presented as this proposition’s exact construction."},"sourceIssues":[]}
